# Migrations that are deliberately NOT applied to production, one id per line.
#
# The bundle stamps how many migrations it expects, and the drift banner fires
# when production has fewer. Counting a migration that is intentionally on the
# shelf makes that warning permanent — and a warning that is always on is one
# nobody reads on the day it is finally true.
#
# They stay in this directory on purpose: tests/database.mjs enumerates the
# folder, and that is the only thing exercising them before they go live.
#
# Remove the line in the same change that applies the migration.
202609090026_intimate_games
#
# Scheduled messages. Shelved on arrival, not because it is unfinished but
# because applying it is a decision about retention: it is the one table in
# this app that holds a message body in plaintext on purpose, for up to a week.
# Apply 202609150040 in the SQL editor, then operations/schedule_scheduled_messages.sql
# standalone (cron statements have aborted batched transactions), and remove the
# line below in the SAME change. Without the cron job the rows accumulate and
# nothing ever sends.
#
# The client half ships either way and hides itself: loadScheduled() tells a
# missing RPC apart from a failed one, so on a database without this migration
# the clock button and the strip simply do not render.
202609150040_scheduled_messages
